{"nagaland":{"id":"06f4a8a2-30ea-4e63-b12a-24df07fcb225","word":"Nagaland","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"state in northeastern India","word":"Nagaland"}],"pos":"name","tags":null,"senses":[{"categories":["English entries with incorrect language header","English lemmas","English proper nouns","English terms suffixed with -land","English uncountable nouns","Entries with translation boxes","Pages with 2 entries","Pages with entries","Terms with Armenian translations","Terms with Assamese translations","Terms with Bengali translations","Terms with Bulgarian translations","Terms with Dhivehi translations","Terms with Finnish translations","Terms with Georgian translations","Terms with Greek translations","Terms with Gujarati translations","Terms with Hebrew translations","Terms with Hindi translations","Terms with Hungarian translations","Terms with Japanese translations","Terms with Kannada translations","Terms with Korean translations","Terms with Latvian translations","Terms with Lithuanian translations","Terms with Malayalam translations","Terms with Mandarin translations","Terms with Marathi translations","Terms with Odia translations","Terms with Persian translations","Terms with Portuguese translations","Terms with Punjabi translations","Terms with Russian translations","Terms with Tamil translations","Terms with Telugu translations","Terms with Thai translations","Terms with Urdu translations","en:Nagaland, India","en:Places in India","en:States and union territories of India"],"links":[["state","state"],["India","India#English"],["Kohima","Kohima#English"]],"glosses":["A state in northeastern India. Capital: Kohima."],"id":"c58c79ba-67d9-4d10-9329-cced2d267d04"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]},"nag":{"id":"f5249ccf-c24a-4eb9-abe2-803110b4e0e2","word":"nag","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"complain about insignificant matters","word":"azucrinar"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"complain about insignificant matters","word":"atazanar"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"complain about insignificant matters","word":"moer o juízo"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"bother with memories","word":"importunar"}],"pos":"verb","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"The room is never cleaned, so her mother nags and nags until she explodes with frustration and threatens to sell her to the lowest bidder.","ref":"2006, Jerry Day, How to Raise Kids You Want to Keep, →ISBN:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[41,45],[50,54]],"id":"7c0344bf-826c-4e59-8f37-3886298ff612"},{"text":"Anyone would think that I nagged at you, Amanda! (From Amanda! by Robin Klein)","id":"8b67857c-d1e1-4954-a72d-4fa3050b6d97"}],"categories":["English intransitive verbs","English terms with quotations","English transitive verbs"],"links":[["remind","remind"],["complain","complain"],["insignificant","insignificant"]],"raw_glosses":["(ambitransitive) To repeatedly remind or complain to (someone) in an annoying way, often about insignificant or unnecessary matters."],"glosses":["To repeatedly remind or complain to (someone) in an annoying way, often about insignificant or unnecessary matters."],"tags":["ambitransitive"],"id":"f15b743a-1b52-4ee4-ba3f-e6b3f8ccd177"},{"examples":[{"text":"The notion that he forgot something nagged him the rest of the day.","bold_text_offsets":[[36,42]],"type":"example","id":"02de2e92-88da-46e0-b70b-6e8983832d23"},{"text":"I guess it happens all the time in crime stories where the detective suddenly remembers a bit of conversation that nags him in some way, then for some inexplicable reason, it's just right there in front of you, like a sign pointing 'here!","ref":"2010, John David Wells, Diamonds of Affection and Other Stories, →ISBN, page 100:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[115,119]],"id":"72dce9bc-eaf9-435a-b1e1-aaebd909c1c3"},{"text":"Sometimes I write because there is a question that nags at me, sometimes because there is a question that nags at other people.","ref":"2010, John Goldingay, Key Questions about Christian Faith: Old Testament Answers, →ISBN:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[51,55],[106,110]],"id":"2c4136ba-398e-4bfa-94d8-1700a9b06f37"},{"text":"You are sleeping on your side in the bed in your flat, heavily embroiled in a dream which sucks and nags at you and makes no sense; an old primary school teacher is there and a cat you have to take to a supermarket; you are in a canoe.","ref":"2013, Ra Page, L.E. Yates, Ann Winter, Parenthesis: A New Generation in Short Fiction:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[100,104]],"id":"53d6994f-5786-494a-bada-34df9b186c60"}],"links":[["persistent","persistent"]],"categories":["English terms with quotations","English terms with usage examples"],"glosses":["To bother with persistent thoughts or memories."],"id":"6a5a94ef-4d61-4a64-937c-1516b7f19d1d"},{"examples":[{"text":"But at night, around the uncertain edge of dreams, and when the wind nags, there are few whom an odd sound will not thrill","ref":"1999, Tim Parks, Adultery and Other Diversions, →ISBN:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[69,73]],"id":"20ec5331-d525-4285-8cf8-15832c035711"},{"text":"When a breeze comes up and nags the surface, it sparkles like a gemstone.","ref":"2013, Tina Egnoski, Perishables, →ISBN:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[27,31]],"id":"2ebb10e0-c5a1-40ce-b5bd-c94a52af13ab"},{"text":"We are well accustomed as we look out upon Nature at close range to see great creatures harrassed^([sic]) by little creatures. The lot of each big one seems to be in the keeping of some little one, which never quits it, nags it, stings it, wears it out, drives it desperate, makes life somewhat a burden to it and death somewhat a relief.","ref":"2014, James Lane Allen, The Last Christmas Tree: An Idyl of Immortality, →ISBN, page 8:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[220,224]],"id":"6beb26a3-801a-4020-970a-fd552b59e58b"},{"text":"a nagging pain in his left knee","id":"cbc03214-d73f-4493-a0a4-68e9641ee1e5"},{"text":"a nagging north wind","id":"bb1c7206-d72b-428c-8247-e071008680b5"}],"categories":["English terms with quotations"],"glosses":["To bother or disturb persistently in any way."],"id":"382a5f64-2d27-4e24-b51a-92d54f650bf0"}],"related":[{"word":"gnaw"}],"synonyms":[{"sense":"continually remind or complain","word":"ride"},{"sense":"continually remind or complain","word":"sit on"},{"sense":"bother with thoughts or memories","word":"haunt"},{"sense":"persistently bother or annoy","word":"worry"}]},"nagasaki":{"id":"6c96fa50-b37a-4b1b-881d-c52930f792d0","word":"Nagasaki","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"Japanese city","tags":["feminine"],"word":"Nagasaki"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"Japanese city","tags":["feminine"],"word":"Nagasáqui"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"Japanese city","tags":["feminine"],"word":"Nangasáqui"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"Japanese city","tags":["feminine"],"word":"Nangasaque"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"Japanese prefecture","tags":["feminine"],"word":"Nagasaki"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"Japanese prefecture","tags":["feminine"],"word":"Nagasáqui"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"Japanese prefecture","tags":["feminine"],"word":"Nangasáqui"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"Japanese prefecture","tags":["feminine"],"word":"Nangasaque"}],"pos":"name","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"VINCENT: Tens of thousands killed before sundown; nobody's killed people that fast since Hiroshima and Nagasaki.","ref":"2004, Stuart Beattie, Collateral, DreamWorks Pictures:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[103,111]],"id":"d73a7601-e185-4c5e-8fde-1080e2c5c999"},{"text":"This slab is where 